details:
(a) the number of Foreign Tourist Arrivals (FTAs), Overseas Citizens of India (OCI) cardholders, Non-Resident Indians (NRIs) and other foreign visitors arriving in India since 2021, category-wise and year-wise;
(b) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised for overseas tourism promotion, branding and marketing of India since 2021 under various schemes and programmes, scheme-wise, country-wise and year-wise; and
(c) the details of promotional campaigns undertaken by Government in foreign countries during the said period, indicating the countries covered and expenditure incurred?

(a) whether Government is considering the proposal for establishment of an Indian Institute of Management (IIM) in Telangana, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the criteria adopted by Government for establishment of new IIMs;
(c) whether Government has assessed the requirement of an IIM in Telangana in view of its industrial, educational and economic significance, if so, the details thereof;
(d) the present status of the proposal, if any, for establishment of an IIM in Telangana; and
(e) the timeline proposed for taking a decision in this regard?

(a) the policy, standards and guidelines prescribed by Government for establishment and operation of crèche facilities in Government establishments, private establishments, factories, commercial establishments and other workplaces;
(b) whether Government has prescribed minimum standards regarding infrastructure, child safety, staffing, caregiver-to-child ratio, nutrition, hygiene, emergency response, CCTV surveillance and health protocols for crèche facilities;
(c) the mechanism for registration, licensing, inspection and periodic monitoring of crèches, indicating the authority responsible for enforcement, State-wise; and
(d) whether any assessment has been undertaken regarding compliance with the prescribed standards by private establishments required to provide crèche facilities under the Maternity Benefit Act, 1961 and other applicable laws?

(a) whether Government has adopted new technologies for the storage, preservation and distribution of foodgrains to reduce post-harvest losses and improve food security;
(b) the details of such technologies, including but not limited to automated grain dispensing systems (such as GrainATMs), hermetic storage technologies, grain moisture meters, smart silos, IoT-based storage monitoring systems and other modern storage solutions; and
(c) the extent to which these technologies have been adopted across the country, including the number of pilot projects, States covered, storage capacity created and the outcomes achieved so far?

(a) whether Government is considering the national project status to the Palamuru-Rangareddy Lift Irrigation Scheme (PRLIS), if so, the details thereof;
(b) the present status of the proposal and the reasons for its acceptance or pendency;
(c) the criteria for declaring an irrigation project as a national project; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the irrigation potential, drought mitigation and drinking water benefits of PRLIS, if so, the details thereof, and the Central assistance proposed for the Project?

(a) the number of food irradiation facilities established and operational, along with their installed and utilised processing capacity in the country, State-wise;
(b) the quantity and types of perishable agricultural commodities, including fruits, vegetables, spices, cereals and other food products, treated through irradiation facilities during the last three years, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) the details of the schemes, financial assistance, subsidy or other incentives for establishing irradiation facilities; and
(d) whether the existing irradiation infrastructure is adequate to meet the country's requirement for preservation and export of perishable commodities, if not, the details of the gap assessment carried out by Government?

(a) the funds sanctioned, released, utilised and pending under various components of the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) for Telangana during the last five years and the current year, component-wise and year-wise;
(b) the details of pending liabilities under MGNREGS in Telangana, including wage payments, material component, administrative expenditure and other dues;
(c) whether Government has withheld or delayed the release of MGNREGS funds to Telangana, if so, the reasons therefor and the corrective measures taken;
(d) whether Government proposes to release all pending dues to Telangana before undertaking complete discontinuation of MGNREGS?

(a) the share of women engaged in agriculture and allied activities in the country, State-wise;
(b) the number and percentage of women engaged in agriculture who own agricultural land either individually or jointly, State-wise;
(c) whether Government recognises women engaged in agriculture but not holding land titles, as farmers for the purpose of Government schemes, institutional credit, crop insurance, compensation and other agricultural benefits;
(d) whether Government is considering any legislative or policy measures to provide formal recognition to women cultivators and tenant women farmers irrespective of land ownership, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the funds allocated, released and utilised under Khelo India Scheme for Telangana during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the sports infrastructure projects sanctioned, completed and under implementation in the State under the scheme, district-wise;
(c) the sports facilities created or upgraded under the scheme in the State;
(d) whether any proposals from the State are pending approval or release of funds under the scheme and if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the steps taken to strengthen sports infrastructure and talent development in the State?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment to determine whether meals served under the PM POSHAN scheme meet the prescribed nutritional standards, in view of National Family Health Survey (NFHS)-6 findings showing 29.3 percent stunting and 31.8 percent underweight prevalence among children;
(b) whether Government has taken note of the omission of anaemia data in NFHS-6 and its implications for PM POSHAN; and
(c) whether Government has taken note of the removal or non-inclusion of eggs by certain States and whether such decisions are based on any scientific, nutritional or public health assessment?

(a) the current demand and availability of certified and quality seeds in the country, crop-wise and State-wise;
(b) the quantity of seeds available with Government agencies, seed corporations, seed banks and private seed producers, crop-wise and State-wise;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of deficient rainfall, El Niño conditions and other adverse weather events on seed production during the current and previous agricultural seasons, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the estimated crop loss and seed production loss reported due to such climatic conditions, crop-wise and State-wise and the compensation mechanism available for seed growers in the last five years, State-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken note of severe air pollution levels in industrial towns across the country, including Byrnihat on Assam–Meghalaya border;
(b) the details of top 50 most polluted cities/towns in the country during the last five years, indicating their annual average PM2.5 and PM10 levels and the major sources of pollution in each case;
(c) whether Government has assessed the role of industrial concentration, transportation, geographical factors and urban planning practices in contributing to severe air pollution in industrial clusters; and
(d) the details of funds allocated and utilised under various schemes for pollution mitigation during the last five years?

(a) the reasons for the continued high prevalence of stunting, wasting and underweight children as reported between NFHS-4 (2015-16) and NFHS-6 (2023-24);
(b) whether Government has assessed the reasons for the limited improvement in child nutrition outcomes despite substantial expenditure under various nutrition schemes and, if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether any social audit, evaluation or impact assessment of Poshan Abhiyaan and related programmes has been conducted to ascertain their effectiveness in reducing child malnutrition and, if so, the findings thereof; and 
(d) the targeted measures to tackle stunting, wasting and underweight and improve nutrition outcomes among children?

(a) whether Government has considered recognising truck drivers as a distinct occupational category under any labour or social security law and if so, details thereof;
(b) whether Government has assessed the coverage of truck drivers under insurance, pension, healthcare, accident compensation and other welfare schemes and the gaps therein;
(c) whether any minimum standards for wages, working hours, mandatory rest periods, roadside facilities and occupational safety have been prescribed for truck drivers; and
(d) whether Government has examined international best practices and regulatory frameworks for truck drivers, for strengthening social security and reducing excessive working hours and if so, the details thereof?
GK

(a) the number of incidents involving the collapse or major structural failure of bridges, roads, tunnels, flyovers and other highway infrastructure on National Highways and State Highways during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the number of persons killed and injured in such incidents, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) whether Government has conducted any technical audit, inquiry or investigation into such incidents and, if so, the details thereof, including the causes identified such as design deficiencies etc.; and
(d) whether responsibility has been fixed and action taken against the agencies, contractors, consultants or officials found responsible, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of food business operators, including manufacturers, traders, street food vendors and small food establishments, registered or licensed under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, and the number of licences and registrations that have expired or not been renewed, State-wise;
(b) the number of cases of food adulteration detected, prosecutions launched and convictions secured during the last five years, State-wise and category-wise; and
(c) the measures taken by Government to bring small & petty food businesses, street food vendors and informal food establishments into the formal food safety and licensing framework?

(a) the exchange rate of the Indian Rupee against the US Dollar in May 2014 and the corresponding exchange rate at present, along with the annual average exchange rate and annual rate of depreciation/appreciation since 2021, year-wise;
(b) the amount of foreign exchange reserves utilised by the Reserve Bank of India through the sale of US Dollars or any other intervention to stabilise the Rupee since 2021, year-wise, along with the net amount of US Dollars purchased and sold during the said period; and
(c) the impact of the depreciation of the Rupee on imports, inflation, external debt servicing and the current account balance?

(a) whether Government has studied international standards, regulations and practices relating to ethanol blending and ethanol-based fuels, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the countries and institutions whose standards and practices have been examined by Government;
(c) whether Government has assessed the suitability of international ethanol standards for Indian climatic, vehicular and fuel conditions, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether any modifications or safeguards have been adopted for India based on international experience and if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the measures taken to ensure that ethanol blending levels adopted in India are safe, sustainable and internationally benchmarked?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the impact of climate change, El Niño conditions, deficient rainfall and erratic monsoon patterns on India's food security and agricultural production, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has estimated the likely impact of the current season's weather conditions on the production of major food crops, if so, the crop-wise and State-wise details thereof; 
(c) whether Government has prepared any contingency plan to address possible shortfalls in foodgrains production arising from adverse climatic conditions, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the list of such vulnerable districts identified, State-wise?

(a) whether Government has prepared district-wise contingency plans to address extreme weather events, climate variability and agricultural distress;
(b) whether any special task force, coordination mechanism or dedicated monitoring body has been constituted at Central level for the implementation, monitoring and periodic review of such contingency plans, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the mechanism adopted for continuous monitoring of climate risks, implementation of contingency measures and coordination among Central Ministries, State Governments and district administrations; and
(d) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised for the implementation of climate adaptation measures in vulnerable districts during the last five years?
bs

(a) whether the Central Government is aware of the proposal of the Government of Telangana to develop Bharat Future City, envisaged as a net-zero, next-generation urban centre;
(b) whether Government has received any proposals or requests from the State Government seeking Central assistance, policy support or clearances for the said project; and
(c) whether any financial, technical or institutional support has been extended or is under consideration of the Central Government for the development of Bharat Future City?

(a) whether Government has received proposals from Government of Telangana for eight new railway line projects, the project-wise details including route length, estimated cost and year of submission;
(b) the present status of clearance of these railway line proposals and the reasons for pendency, including whether these proposals are awaiting feasibility approval, budgetary support or inter-ministerial clearances; and
(c) whether proposals relating to Hyderabad Metro Rail Phase-II, including Phases IIA and IIB, with an estimated project cost of ?44,000 crore, to be shared equally by the Centre and the State, have been submitted to the Ministry?

(a) whether Government has assessed the mismatch between sectors where training is provided under Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) and sectors where actual labour demand exists, in view of projections that over 60 per cent of job demand is in sectors such as construction, logistics and hospitality;
(b) whether the apparel sector alone accounts for about 28.4 per cent of total certifications under PMKVY despite relatively weak job growth in that sector;
(c) the sector-wise number of persons trained, certified and placed in jobs under PMKVY during the last five years; and
(d) whether limited industry participation in curriculum design, financing and certification has affected employability outcomes?

(a) whether Government has assessed the national requirement of ambulances based on population, geography and emergency response norms and the details thereof;
(b) the total number of ambulances currently operational in the country, including Basic Life Support (BLS), Advanced Life Support (ALS), Government-run and private ambulances, State-wise;
(c) whether there exists a gap between required and available ambulances, particularly in rural, tribal and remote areas and the extent of such gap; and
(d) whether any national or State-level audits or evaluations have been conducted to assess the response time, coverage, staffing, equipment availability and effectiveness of ambulance services?
K

(a) the year-wise allocation, actual expenditure and outstanding dues under the urea subsidy during the last five years;
(b) whether it is a fact that the urea subsidy has been reduced in the current financial year despite reported shortages of fertilizers across several States during peak agricultural seasons and the reasons therefor;
(c) whether the reduction in subsidy has contributed to supply constraints, higher black-marketing or increased hardship for farmers; and
(d) the current status of nano urea, including year-wise production, distribution, farmer adoption, crop-wise and State-wise usage and evidence of its effectiveness in reducing conventional urea demand?

(a) the total number of proposals received from the State Government of Telangana since 2023 for the development of Hyderabad as a global city, including infrastructure, transport, urban renewal and smart city initiatives;
(b) the number of such proposals approved, partially approved or rejected, proposal-wise and year-wise;
(c) the details of proposals presently pending with the Central Government or its committees, along with the reasons for pendency;
(d) the financial assistance or approvals granted, if any, for such projects; and
(e) whether any timeline has been fixed for disposal of the pending proposals?

(a) whether Government has received proposals from Government of Telangana for the development of airports at Adilabad, Palvancha and Basant Nagar (Ramagundam);
(b) the current status of these proposals, including whether they are pending at the level of Government, Airports Authority of India (AAI);
(c) the reasons for non-approval of these airport proposals so far, including whether issues relate to technical feasibility, land availability, airspace constraints, financial viability or inter-ministerial clearances; and
(d) whether Government has conducted or proposes to conduct any feasibility studies for airports at Adilabad, Palvancha and Basant Nagar (Ramagundam), if so, the details and timelines thereof?

(a) the total number of reported instances of data breaches, leaks or cyber attacks involving Aadhaar data or other major Government databases since 2021, year-wise;
(b) the action taken in each such case, including investigations, penalties and corrective cybersecurity measures;
(c) whether Government has assessed the risks arising from shifting the Census to a fully digital, app- and web-based data collection system covering over one billion citizens; and
(d) the cybersecurity architecture and safeguards proposed for the digital Census, including encryption, access control, device security and data storage within sovereign Government infrastructure?

(a) the number of Memoranda of Understandings (MoUs) signed during the Prime Minister’s foreign visits since 2021, year-wise and country-wise;
(b) the details of such MoUs, including defence, energy, trade, technology, infrastructure, health and education, sector-wise;
(c) the current status of implementation of these MoUs, indicating the MoUs fully implemented, partially implemented, or remain unimplemented;
(d) the reasons for delay or non-materialisation of MoUs that have not progressed beyond signing; and
(e) whether Government has undertaken any review or monitoring mechanism to track outcomes of MoUs signed during high-level visits?

(a) whether Government has received proposals from Government of Telangana for the Regional Ring Road (RRR) project, including a request for Union Cabinet approval and Central funding amounting to ?34,367.62 crore;
(b) whether proposals seeking sanction of ?45,000 crore for ten greenfield radial roads connecting the Outer Ring Road (ORR) with the RRR have been submitted to the Ministry and the stage at which these proposals are currently pending; and
(c) whether the Ministry has received a proposal for approval and funding of approximately ?17,000 crore for the Bandar Port–Dry Port greenfield highway and the reasons for non-approval, so far?

(a) the customs duty rates (basic customs duty, social welfare surcharge and any other applicable levies) imposed on adult diapers during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) whether the customs duty on adult diapers has been increased or altered in the Union Budget 2026–27, the details thereof;
(c) the rationale for increasing customs duty on an essential healthcare and hygiene product largely used by senior citizens, Persons with Disabilities and patients with chronic illnesses; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the impact of such duty changes on affordability for elderly and low-income households with limited or fixed incomes?

(a) whether the Central Government has received and examined the proposal for Hyderabad Metro Rail Phase-II, if so, since when the proposal has been pending with the Centre;
(b) the reasons for the delay in granting in-principle or final approval to the project, despite submission and its stated importance for urban mobility in a major metropolitan city;
(c) whether the proposal is stalled at any specific level within the Central Government, including inter-ministerial consultations or appraisal committees; and
(d) whether the Central Government has sought clarifications or imposed additional conditions that have contributed to the delay, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the cost charged from passengers for meals in premium express trains such as Vande Bharat and other similar services, train-wise and class-wise;
(b) the percentage of the total ticket fare attributable to food charges;
(c) the actual cost incurred by Indian Railways or its catering agencies in providing such meals and the margin, if any, charged from passengers;
(d) whether any audit or independent assessment has been conducted on the pricing, quality, hygiene and nutritional standards of meals served on these trains; and
(e) the number of complaints received from passengers regarding food quality and overpricing during the last three years, train-wise?

(a) the number of elephant deaths caused by collisions with trains and road vehicles across the country since 2021, State-wise and year-wise along with the number and location of identified collision hotspots;
(b) the mitigation measures implemented at such hotspots, including fencing, underpasses/overpasses, speed restrictions, animal detection systems and night patrolling, State-wise;
(c) the length of railway tracks and roads that have been fenced or secured to prevent elephant movement onto tracks or carriageways, State-wise;
(d) the total length of railway lines covered by Artificial Intelligence (AI)-based warning systems; and
(e) whether any independent evaluation has been conducted to assess the effectiveness of AI-based system?
v

(a) whether Government has granted financial and cabinet approvals for the commencement of works on the Regional Ring Road (RRR) project in Telangana;
(b) whether approvals have been accorded separately for the northern and southern sections of the RRR and the present status of each segment;
(c) the total estimated project cost and the financial assistance or funding pattern approved by the Centre; and
(d) whether any component of the project is pending for approval, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the ?8,000 crore allocated by the Fifteenth Finance Commission for development of eight new cities has remained largely unutilised for nearly five years;
(b) the State/UT-wise details of proposals received and the status of their appraisal;
(c) the reasons for not sanctioning or initiating any new city project despite fund availability;
(d) whether gaps in design, guidelines, Inter-Ministerial coordination or Centre–State engagement have caused the delay; and
(e) the timeline for project approvals or reallocation of funds to prevent lapse without tangible outcomes?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government announced the creation of a ?1 lakh crore Urban Challenge Fund for urban infrastructure and governance reforms;
(b) the amount of funds allocated, released and utilised under the said Fund so far, year-wise, since its announcement;
(c) whether the Urban Challenge Fund has become fully operational and if not, the present status of its institutional and operational framework; and
(d) the reasons for the delay in operationalising and implementing the Urban Challenge Fund, including delays in framing guidelines, securing Cabinet or financial approvals or coordination with States?

(a) the overall trend in disposal of RTI requests since 2021, including the number of applications disposed of, partially answered, transferred or remaining unresolved, year-wise;
(b) whether Government has analysed the grounds on which information has been refused, particularly the use of personal information exemptions and the year-wise frequency of such refusals;
(c) the broad categories of public authorities or sectors where requests for information are most frequently denied and the proportion of such denials in relation to total RTI applications; and
(d) the current pendency position of second appeals and complaints before the Central Information Commission and average time taken for disposal?

(a) whether it is a fact that cases of cyber fraud and financial fraud have increased sharply in the country since 2021, year-wise;
(b) the total number of reported cyber frauds, banking frauds, digital payment frauds and other financial frauds, along with the total amount of money lost, year-wise since 2021;
(c) whether Government has assessed the reasons behind the rise in cyber frauds, including rapid digitisation, weak cyber awareness, poor grievance redressal, delayed response and cross-border criminal networks; and
(d) whether it is a fact that a large proportion of fraud amounts remain unrecovered, if so, details of total amount recovered vis-à-vis losses incurred, year-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken note of recent enforcement actions by food safety authorities involving detection and confiscation of adulterated, contaminated or unsafe food products;
(b) the procedure followed in detection, including sampling, laboratory testing, re-testing (if any) and final determination of food items as unsafe or unfit for consumption;
(c) the mechanism for custody and secure storage of such food items once declared unsafe and the authorities responsible for their supervision during this period; and
(d) the process adopted for disposal or destruction of unsafe food products, including the agencies involved and safeguards to ensure environmental and public health safety?

(a) the total number of pending bills under the Ex-Servicemen Contributory Health Scheme (ECHS) for empanelled hospitals and individual beneficiaries, year-wise, since 2020, the reasons for such delays;
(b) whether retired soldiers face difficulties in accessing healthcare under ECHS due to a shortage of funds, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the total number of ex-servicemen, including Emergency Commissioned Officers, Short Service Officers and jawans, who have been denied pension benefits despite completing eligible service; and
(d) whether Government acknowledges concerns that decisions related to the 8th CPC will directly impact the future pay and pensions of over 25 lakh veterans?

(a) the extent of land-use change involving agricultural land during the five years, including diversion for industrial, urban, infrastructure or other non-farm purposes, State/UT-wise;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the drivers behind such land-use changes, including urbanisation, industrial expansion, infrastructure projects or real estate development;
(c) whether the impact of reduction in cultivable land on food production, farm incomes and rural employment has been evaluated, if so, the findings thereof; and
(d) the area of degraded, fallow or wasteland that has been reclaimed, restored or brought under cultivation during the same period, along with the schemes under which such work was undertaken?

(a) the number of women gig and platform workers registered in the country, State-wise;
(b) the social security schemes and provisions currently applicable to women gig workers, including health insurance, accident cover, old-age protection and maternity benefits;
(c) whether any specific maternity benefit or paid leave provisions exist for women gig workers under the Code on Social Security, 2020 or any other scheme and if so, the details thereof;
(d) the extent of coverage and benefits actually provided to women gig workers under such schemes so far, year-wise; and
(e) the gaps in social security coverage, particularly maternity support and income security, for women gig workers?

(a) the number of permissions/approvals granted by the Central Government for tree felling and forest diversion during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the area of forest land diverted for infrastructure, industrial, mining, energy, transport, urban development and other projects during the said period, year-wise and project-wise;
(c) the number of trees approved for felling and the number of trees actually felled, year-wise during the said period;
(d) the break-up of forest diversion and tree felling approvals during the said period, State-wise; and
(e) whether Government has assessed the cumulative environmental impact of such large-scale tree felling and forest diversion?

(a) the details of the funds allocated under Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) for the State of Telangana, as per the Central Government's share; 
(b) the initial target of JJM for Telangana and total household tap water connections provided, district-wise; 
(c) nation-wide amount lost to the public exchequer due to such irregularities, if so, the amount involved, State-wise; 
(d) whether any penalties, recoveries, blacklisting of contractors, or disciplinary action have been initiated against various irregularities as reported by media; and
(e) whether funds under the JJM have been withheld, reduced, or delayed for certain States including Telangana?

(a) total number of airports, heliports constructed, revived or inaugurated under the UDAN (Ude Desh ka Aam Naagrik) scheme it started in 2016 during last five years, State-wise and year-wise;
(b) total number of airports presently operational with regular commercial flight services and those that are non-operational, along with the reasons thereof;
(c) airports where flight operations commenced under UDAN but subsequently discontinued, duration of operations and reasons for discontinuation;
(d) airports where no commercial flight has taken off until date; and
(e) total expenditure incurred on management and upkeep of non-operational airports since their existence under the UDAN scheme, airport-wise and year-wise?

(a) the details of cotton production in the country during the last five years, State-wise;
(b) the details of cotton exports to the United States from each State during the last five years, along with the revenue earned;
(c) the total number of cotton farmers in the country, State-wise;
(d) the steps taken by Government to protect the cotton farmers and exporters, including any relief or support package announced for affected States in the wake of US tariffs; and
(e) whether Government has also assessed the impact of scrapping of 11 percent import duty on cotton imports into India on domestic cotton farmers?

(a) the total number of districts currently classified as Left-Wing Extremism (LWE)-affected or partially affected, State-wise;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any independent assessment to evaluate the ground situation in these districts beyond the data received from State administrations;
(c) whether there exists any dedicated long-term rehabilitation, development and reconstruction plan for districts affected by LWE, particularly those where extremism has been eliminated or significantly reduced; and
(d) the details of funds allocated, released, and actually utilised under all schemes aimed at rehabilitation and development of LWE-affected districts in the last five years, year-wise and State-wise?

(a) the detailed procedure prescribed for Indian students who pursue medical education in foreign countries and subsequently return to India to practice medicine;
(b) the manner in which the compulsory internship is regulated for Foreign Medical Graduates (FMGs) before granting them a licence to practice;
(c) whether the current regulatory provisions are sufficient to ensure that Indian medical graduates and FMGs are at par once they complete their internship and begin service; and
(d) whether there is any proposal to modify the licensing requirements for FMGs, such as increasing the duration of the mandatory rural internship?

(a) the total volume and value of shrimp exports from India to the United States during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) whether there has been any decline in shrimp exports to the US due to import restrictions, disease outbreaks or price fluctuations, if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has identified new export markets to diversify shrimp trade and reduce dependency;
(d) the total financial assistance, subsidies or export incentives extended to shrimp farmers and exporters under various schemes during the last five years; and
(e) the steps taken to support shrimp farmers affected due to declined production and trade issues?

(a) the number of proposals received for clearances of highways, railway tracks and other physical infrastructure projects through eco-sensitive zones, wildlife corridors, national parks and tiger reserves;
(b) the number of wild animal deaths of elephants, tigers and leopards recorded due to railway collisions and road accidents during the last three years, State-wise and species-wise;
(c) the details of railway and highway stretches identified as high-risk for wildlife movement, along with the mitigation measures; and
(d) the number of dedicated wildlife overpasses, underpasses, eco-ducts, canopy bridges, fencing systems or speed-control interventions constructed, so far, on such sensitive stretches?

(a) whether Government is aware that a significant number of women are being classified as ‘employed’ even when they are engaged in unpaid or informal household-based work;
(b) the criteria adopted by Government to define ‘employment’ in such cases and whether unpaid labour is being inaccurately counted as gainful employment;
(c) whether data indicates a rise in unpaid labour among women in recent years, particularly in rural areas and if so, the reasons for this disturbing trend; and
(d) the reasons for persistent long-term decline in women’s labour force participation, despite various Government schemes claiming to promote women employment?

(a) whether it is a fact that children’s learning outcomes across the country are yet to return to pre-COVID-19 levels, particularly in reading, writing and arithmetic skills;
(b) the reasons for the continued gap in learning outcomes despite the implementation of various flagship programmes such as Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan and PM e-Vidya;
(c) the details of steps taken by Government to re-enroll children who dropped out during the COVID-19 period and ensure their reintegration into the school system; and
(d) the total funds allocated and utilised during last five years under various remedial learning and bridge education programmes to address post-pandemic learning loss?

(a) the details of penetration of women’s health insurance coverage including those from low-income and unorganised sectors in the country, disaggregated by rural and urban regions;
(b) whether Government proposes to introduce additional tax benefits or incentives for households purchasing individual health insurance policies, specifically for Female members;
(c) the initiatives undertaken by Government to promote health insurance awareness and enrolment among women, particularly in rural and aspirational districts; and
(d) whether Government is considering any special insurance products or partnerships with private insurers to improve women-centric health coverage?

(a) the number of railway stations identified for redevelopment across the country, along with number of projects currently ongoing and those completed, State-wise;
(b) the mechanism adopted by Government for redevelopment of stations, and whether such projects are being implemented under Public-Private Partnership (PPP);
(c) whether the redeveloped stations are leased or handed over to private developers for a fixed period after completion, if so, the details thereof including lease terms and revenue-sharing arrangements;
(d) the total funds allocated, released, and utilised for station redevelopment projects during the last five years, year-wise; and
(e) the amenities and facilities mandated under redevelopment plan?

(a) the total tourist footfalls since 2019 and whether it has reached the pre-pandemic levels and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether it is a fact that the budget allocation for overseas promotion and Market Development Assistance (MDA) has been slashed during the last five years and if so, the details thereof, year-wise;
(c) the manner in which various civic schemes, including Swachh Bharat Mission and Smart Cities Mission have contributed to promoting and supporting tourism in the country; and 
(d) whether Government has issued any advisory to States regarding the security concerns that are affecting foreign tourists perception about the country and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total number of missing children reported, traced and recovered in the country during each of the last five years, State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) whether there has been an increase in the number of missing child cases in recent years, if so, the reasons identified by Government;
(c) the agencies, initiatives and mechanisms responsible for tracing missing children, including coordination among police;
(d) the total funds allocated, released, and utilised for programmes aimed at locating and rehabilitating missing children during the last five years; and
(e) the steps taken by Government to further strengthen the mechanism to tackle the challenges of missing children?

