THE MINISTER OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JANESHWAR MISHRA):
(a) Under the National Hydrology Project (renamed as Hydrology Project), the details of the
Projects/programmes proposed to be taken up with World Bank assistance in Andhra Pradesh are as
under:
(i) Improvements to the observation systems;
(ii) Establishment of interactive computerised data banks and inter-bank and inter-bank
communication systems;
(iii) Improvements in reservoir instrumentation and management;
(iv) Improvements in the monitoring of return flows from selected irrigated command areas;
(v) Real time water resources management by extending the flood warnings/forecasting system by
supplementing five existing wireless stations which have been installed for flood management by
20 additional stations;
(vi) Institutional strengthening activities;
(vii) Procurement of equipment and material.
(b) These activities are proposed to be completed in a period of six years with the credit
closing date of the Project as December 31, 2001.

